From: Mo Werk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Sat, 16 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] amplifiers: cs40l26: drive reset by physical level

sol builds this driver from the pixel-watch branch (aurora's working
reference for the same CS40L26A) but boots its own stock device tree,
and the two disagree on which logical value releases reset:

    seluna     (sol's stock driver)  set_value(reset, 0) releases
    pixel-watch (this driver)        set_value(reset, 1) releases

Each is self-consistent with the DT it shipped with -- sol declares
reset-gpios ... GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW, aurora declares GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH -- so
both land on a physically high line, which is what the part needs: RESET
is active low on the CS40L26A.

Combining sol's DT with this driver inverts twice and holds the line low,
i.e. keeps the chip in reset. The first register access after the pulse
then finds nothing on the bus:

    cs40l26 0-0043: Failed to configure PLL
    cs40l26: probe of 0-0043 failed with error -110

set_pll_loop() is the first control-port access in probe, ahead of the
DEVID read, so no chip ID is ever logged.

Use the raw accessors for the reset line. Polarity is a property of the
part, not of the board, so expressing the pulse in physical levels is
correct for either DT flag and leaves aurora's behaviour unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [sol-specific DT/driver pairing; upstream
carries one driver per branch and each matches its own DT]

Signed-off-by: Mo Werk <mo@mowerk.net>
---
 private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26.c b/private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26.c
--- a/private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26.c
+++ b/private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26.c
@@ -4880,10 +4880,12 @@
 		goto err;
 	}

+	gpiod_set_raw_value_cansleep(cs40l26->reset_gpio, 0);
+
 	usleep_range(CS40L26_MIN_RESET_PULSE_WIDTH,
 			CS40L26_MIN_RESET_PULSE_WIDTH + 100);

-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(cs40l26->reset_gpio, 1);
+	gpiod_set_raw_value_cansleep(cs40l26->reset_gpio, 1);

 	usleep_range(CS40L26_CONTROL_PORT_READY_DELAY,
 			CS40L26_CONTROL_PORT_READY_DELAY + 100);
@@ -4999,7 +5001,7 @@
 	if (va_consumer)
 		regulator_disable(va_consumer);

-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(cs40l26->reset_gpio, 0);
+	gpiod_set_raw_value_cansleep(cs40l26->reset_gpio, 0);

 	if (cs40l26->vibe_init_success) {
 #if !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_INPUT_CS40L26_ATTR_UNDER_BUS)
